! 64 waters at liquid density in a 12.43 Angstrom cell. Every other cell in
! this directory holds 6 or 9 atoms in a box where each domain ends up seeing
! the whole system, so the owned, ghost and outer tiers are indistinguishable
! there and a bug in how they are separated cannot show up. Here the cell is
! three cutoffs across, so a decomposed run gives each domain a genuinely
! smaller owned set than its ghost shell, and the tiering has to be right for
! the energy to come out unchanged.
&GLOBAL
  PRINT_LEVEL LOW
  PROJECT sym_h2o_box
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY_FORCE
&END GLOBAL

&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD FIST
  STRESS_TENSOR ANALYTICAL
  &MM
    &FORCEFIELD
      &NONBONDED
        &MACE
          ATOMS H O
          BACKEND SYMMETRIX
          ! Committed toy MACE model (untrained, deterministic weights); see
          ! README.md in this directory for the generation recipe.
          POT_FILE_NAME Symmetrix/toy_mace-1-8.json
        &END MACE
      &END NONBONDED
    &END FORCEFIELD
    &POISSON
      &EWALD
        EWALD_TYPE none
      &END EWALD
    &END POISSON
  &END MM
  &PRINT
    &FORCES
    &END FORCES
    &STRESS_TENSOR
    &END STRESS_TENSOR
  &END PRINT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      ABC [angstrom] 12.4296 12.4296 12.4296
      PERIODIC XYZ
    &END CELL
    &COORD
